--- Rosetta Code: Closures/Value capture
--- https://rosettacode.org/wiki/Closures/Value_capture
--- Crow has no closures or anonymous functions, by design: a function sees only
--- its parameters. What a closure would keep is kept in the open instead, as a
--- compiler keeps it: each of the ten is a record holding its own copy of i, and
--- `run` is the body they share. The copy is taken when the record is made, so
--- the counter moving on afterwards changes none of them.

struct Square [i]

--- the shared body: the square of the i this one captured
fn run[f]
    return f.i * f.i

functions = []
i = 0
while i lt 10
    functions = push[functions, Square[i]]
    i = i + 1

for k in range[9]
    log['function `k` answers `run[functions[k]]`']
log['(the counter i is now `i`)']
